## 4. IFF container

Sources: `swg_iff/reader.py`, `swg_iff/writer.py`, evidence pack lines 17–20 / 30–31.

### 4.1 Block header grammar (all blocks)

| Off | Size | Type | Endian | Field | Meaning |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| 0 | 4 | `uint32` | **BE** | `tag` | Block tag | ```104:105:swg_iff/reader.py``` |
| 4 | 4 | `uint32` | **BE** | `length` | Payload length **after** this 8-byte header | ```104:105:swg_iff/reader.py``` |

`HEADER_SIZE = 8` ```55:55:swg_iff/reader.py```  
On-disk block span: `[offset .. offset + 8 + length)` ```178:179:swg_iff/reader.py```

### 4.2 FORM block

| Component | Size | Endian | Content | Source |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Header tag | 4 | BE | `TAG_FORM` (`FORM`) | ```106:106:swg_iff/reader.py``` |
| Header length | 4 | BE | `4 + len(children)` — **includes** 4-byte form type | ```131:131:swg_iff/reader.py``` · ```39:41:swg_iff/writer.py``` |
| Form type | 4 | BE | e.g. `MESH`, `0005` | ```112:113:swg_iff/reader.py``` |
| Children | `length − 4` | — | Nested blocks | ```131:134:swg_iff/reader.py``` |

Writer serialization: ```39:41:swg_iff/writer.py```  
Minimum FORM length: 4 (must contain form type) ```110:111:swg_iff/reader.py```

### 4.3 Chunk block

| Component | Size | Endian | Content | Source |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Header tag | 4 | BE | Chunk fourCC | ```104:105:swg_iff/reader.py``` |
| Header length | 4 | BE | Payload only (no type word) | ```104:105:swg_iff/reader.py``` |
| Payload | `length` | — | Opaque bytes | ```157:158:swg_iff/reader.py``` |

Writer: ```34:36:swg_iff/writer.py```

### 4.4 Nesting / navigation invariants (reader)

| Invariant | Rule | Source |
|---|---|---|
| Parent consumption | `used += 8 + block.length` on enter/skip | ```133:133:swg_iff/reader.py``` · ```156:156:swg_iff/reader.py``` |
| FORM child extent | `payload_len = block.length - 4`; child frame `[data_offset .. data_offset + payload_len)` | ```131:134:swg_iff/reader.py``` |
| End-of-form | `frame.used >= frame.length` | ```84:84:swg_iff/reader.py``` |
| Chunk read bound | Reads cannot exceed chunk `frame.length` | ```189:193:swg_iff/reader.py``` |

### 4.5 Chunk payload scalar endianness (inside chunk)

| Scalar reads | Endian | Source |
|---|---|---|
| `read_int16/32`, `read_uint16/32`, `read_float`, vectors | **LE** | ```51:52:swg_iff/reader.py``` · ```209:222:swg_iff/reader.py``` |
| Writer chunk scalars | **LE** | ```14:31:swg_iff/writer.py``` |
| `read_string` | NUL-terminated bytes, no endian | ```227:235:swg_iff/reader.py``` |
| Writer strings | ASCII + `0x00` | ```88:89:swg_iff/writer.py``` |

### 4.6 `validate_iff` size-consistency invariants

Port of `IffNamespace::isValid` ```250:251:swg_iff/reader.py```

| Check | Condition | Source |
|---|---|---|
| Header fits parent | `pos + 8 <= end` | ```255:256:swg_iff/reader.py``` |
| Length non-negative | `block_length >= 0` | ```259:259:swg_iff/reader.py``` |
| Block fits parent | `pos + 8 + block_length <= end` | ```259:259:swg_iff/reader.py``` |
| Sibling advance | `pos = payload + block_length` (= `pos + 8 + block_length`) | ```266:266:swg_iff/reader.py``` |
| FORM recursion | If `tag == TAG_FORM`: walk `[payload+4 .. payload+4+(block_length−4))` when `sub > 0` | ```262:265:swg_iff/reader.py``` |
| Root walk | `walk(0, len(data))` | ```269:269:swg_iff/reader.py``` |

**Failure mode for oversized FORM (evidence pack, not implemented in cited TRE files):**

| Item | Detail | Source |
|---|---|---|
| Corruption class | FORM `length` declared **larger** than bytes available within parent extent | evidence L17–18 |
| Symptom | Validator fails `pos + 8 + block_length > end` ```259:259:swg_iff/reader.py``` | |
| Repair rule (evidence) | Bottom-up **clamp-to-parent-extent** then **recursive validate** pass | evidence L19–20 |
| Clamp formula (derived from validator + evidence) | At block at `pos` with parent end `end`: if `pos + 8 + block_length > end`, set `block_length := end - pos - 8`; rewrite BE length at `pos+4`; if FORM, recurse into clamped child span | evidence L19–20 · validator ```259:265:swg_iff/reader.py``` |
| Provenance | Repaired 102 files (ILM `.skt` strip-tool case); zero failures reported | evidence L19–20 · `SAIS-PR-QUEUE.md` L593–598 |

No `repair_iff` / clamp implementation exists in `tre_reader.py`, `tre_decrypt.py`, or `swg_iff/reader.py` (grep: no matches in repo).

